# Designed Database of MR Brain Images of Healthy Volunteers

Bullitt, Elizabeth; Smith, J Keith; Lin, Weili. CASILab, Department of
Surgery, The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill.

MR images of the brain of 100 healthy subjects, 20 per decade (18-29,
30-39, 40-49, 50-59, 60+), each group equally divided by sex, excluding
subjects with a history of diabetes, hypertension, head trauma,
psychiatric disease, or other conditions likely to affect the brain. The
source mentions an additional 8 subjects (claustrophobia, unexpected
abnormalities or motion during some acquisitions); 109 subject folders
(Normal-001 to Normal-109) are distributed. Images were acquired
on a 3T scanner (Siemens) under standardized protocols. All subjects
provided signed consent allowing images to be made publicly available.

This BIDS version was generated by brainspresso from the MetaImage
(`.mha`) files hosted on https://data.kitware.com (collection
"ITKTubeTK - Bullitt - Healthy MR Database"):

* `sub-<id>/anat/sub-<id>_acq-flash_T1w.nii.gz`: T1 (3D FLASH), 1 mm
* `sub-<id>/anat/sub-<id>_acq-mprage_T1w.nii.gz`: T1 (MPRAGE), 1 mm
* `sub-<id>/anat/sub-<id>_T2w.nii.gz`: T2 (TSE), 1 mm
* `sub-<id>/anat/sub-<id>_angio.nii.gz`: time-of-flight MRA,
  0.5 x 0.5 x 0.8 mm

Sidecars (`*.json`) come from the sample DICOM headers distributed with
the dataset (one per sequence), not from each subject's own scan.

`participants.tsv` was transcribed from the PDF distributed with the
dataset (`Administration/Adjunct information/NormalDatabase2.pdf`): age,
sex, race, handedness, vessel tree quality and remarks, including
incidental findings and family relationships. Subjects 100-109 are not
described in that PDF. `exclude_suggested` marks subjects that the PDF
suggests not using.

## Not converted

The diffusion images (`DTI/*.mha`, 6 directions, b=1000) are distributed
as 3D volumes in which the 7 diffusion volumes are stacked along the
slice axis, without the gradient table (and with an incorrect slice
spacing). Without the gradient directions they cannot be converted to
BIDS `dwi`. `bx bullitt harvest --keys dwi` downloads the original files
to `sourcedata/`.
